# "One mana of any type that land produced" is a type the land's own mana ability produced (CR 106.12a, 605.1b; Zendikar
# Resurgent's and Heartbeat of Spring's rulings), not mana another triggered mana ability added for the same tap. With
# Yavimaya, Cradle of Growth every land is a Forest, so Nissa, Who Shakes the World adds an additional {G} for the basic
# Mountain tapped for {R}; Lavaleaper's mana is still of the Mountain's one type, {R}, so it is added with no question
# (`! Bot1.Modes`) - had Nissa's {G} counted, Bot1 would be asked to choose between {R} and {G}. The pool is {R}{R}{G}.
# Lavaleaper comes on turn 1 (Black Lotus and the Mountain), Nissa on turn 3 (a Forest tapped under Lavaleaper and a
# second Lotus).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Lavaleaper
Forest
Black Lotus
Nissa, Who Shakes the World
Yavimaya, Cradle of Growth
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lavaleaper.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {G}{G}
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Nissa, Who Shakes the World.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Yavimaya, Cradle of Growth.Play
! Bot1.Modes
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate(Ability: {R})
? Bot1.Mana = {R}{R}{G}

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Lavaleaper; Mountain; Nissa, Who Shakes the World; Yavimaya, Cradle of Growth
